more opportunities for lethal encounters, into Black neighborhoods specifically." That's well-documented (broken windows policing, "hot spot" policing models disproportionately targeting Black and Latino neighborhoods) and it's a policy choice that can be — and in some cities has been — changed, unlike "individual character," which isn't a policy lever at all. So I'd say: yes, this pattern is real and damning, and it's exactly the kind of systemic mechanism I've been pointing to the whole conversation — not a rebuttal to it.
